id:                     E380
trigger_tool: cmake|conan|ctest
phase: configuration|test
error_signature: Problem parsing /proc/meminfo|ITK_COMPUTER_MEMORY_SIZE.*empty|ITK_COMPUTER_MEMORY_SIZE is required for runnable OHOS tests|tests passed.*out of 617
severity: 3
category:               cmake, memory, capability-binding, test-inventory
match_keywords: ITK_COMPUTER_MEMORY_SIZE, cmake_host_system_information, TOTAL_PHYSICAL_MEMORY, MemTotal, CTest inventory
title: Bind a validated memory budget when target CMake cannot parse procfs
root_cause: A target can expose valid MemTotal data while CMake's platform-specific host-memory parser fails, causing memory-gated tests to disappear from the generated inventory.
affected_scope: CMake projects that derive conditional test inventory from cmake_host_system_information on targets whose procfs format is not recognized, including same-machine target CI where Conan can_run is true but no task controller exports a memory override.
verification_cmd: Give a validated explicit override highest priority; otherwise, only for runnable targets, parse exactly one local MemTotal kB field, derive the bounded test budget, require the generated cache value, and compare the exact CTest inventory against the host baseline.
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: validated-explicit-memory-budget
rec_description: Keep the full expected inventory, prefer a sealed range-checked override when supplied, and otherwise derive the value from local read-only MemTotal only when the target is runnable.
rec_command: Reject missing, duplicate, nonnumeric, zero, too-small, wrong-unit and implausibly large values; divide KiB to MiB before multiplying by 80; never inspect host procfs for non-runnable cross builds; then bind ITK_COMPUTER_MEMORY_SIZE and require the gated test.
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: conan-cmake-cache-variable-and-target-meminfo-parser
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach:
fallback_description:
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl:
forbid_1_pattern: expected-count.*617|BUILD_TESTING.*OFF|__OHOS__|HarmonyOS
forbid_1_reason: Lowering the expected test count, disabling tests, or branching on a platform name hides the failed capability discovery.
forbid_1_consequence: The package can report success while silently omitting a memory-gated upstream test.
principles:
causes: []
caused_by: []
similar_to: []
conflicts_with: []
prerequisite_of: []
